From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: cs35l45: name the DSP firmware by the DT cirrus,dsp-part-name

The driver hard-codes the wm_adsp part name "cs35l45", so every amplifier
requests cirrus/cs35l45-dsp1-spk-prot.{wmfw,bin}. The ROG Phone 5 has two
CS35L45 with separate speaker-protection tunings (the vendor ZS673KS DT
sets cirrus,dsp-part-name = "cs35l45-rcv" and "cs35l45-spk"; the vendor
partition ships cs35l45-{rcv,spk}-dsp1-spk-{prot,cali}.{wmfw,bin}), so
with one part name both amplifiers would run the same amplifier's tuning.

Read the part name from the optional cirrus,dsp-part-name property and
keep "cs35l45" without it. The per-amplifier files are then
cirrus/cs35l45-rcv-dsp1-spk-prot.{wmfw,bin} and
cirrus/cs35l45-spk-dsp1-spk-prot.{wmfw,bin}; boards without the property
are unchanged. With the property the .bin is mandatory (bin_mandatory):
a board tuning must never run without it, and the dsp_part_named flag lets
later patches scope board-specific behaviour.

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cirrus,cs35l45.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/cirrus,cs35l45.yaml
@@ -53,6 +53,13 @@
     maximum: 3
     default: 2
 
+  cirrus,dsp-part-name:
+    description:
+      Part name used in the DSP firmware file names, for boards that tune
+      each amplifier separately, e.g. "cs35l45-spk" selects
+      cirrus/cs35l45-spk-dsp1-spk-prot.wmfw and .bin. Defaults to "cs35l45".
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/string
+
 patternProperties:
   "^cirrus,gpio-ctrl[1-3]$":
     description:
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l45.h
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l45.h
@@ -493,6 +493,7 @@
 	struct regulator *vdd_a;
 	bool initialized;
 	bool sysclk_set;
+	bool dsp_part_named;
 	u8 slot_width;
 	u8 slot_count;
 	int amplifier_mode;
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l45.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/cs35l45.c
@@ -1382,9 +1382,24 @@
 static int cs35l45_dsp_init(struct cs35l45_private *cs35l45)
 {
 	struct wm_adsp *dsp = &cs35l45->dsp;
+	const char *part;
 	int ret;
 
-	dsp->part = "cs35l45";
+	/*
+	 * Boards with a tuning per amplifier name the firmware by part, as the
+	 * vendor DT does ("cs35l45-rcv", "cs35l45-spk"): the amplifiers then load
+	 * cirrus/cs35l45-rcv-dsp1-spk-prot.{wmfw,bin} and
+	 * cirrus/cs35l45-spk-dsp1-spk-prot.{wmfw,bin}. Without the property both
+	 * would load cs35l45-dsp1-spk-prot.bin, one amplifier's tuning.
+	 */
+	if (device_property_read_string(cs35l45->dev, "cirrus,dsp-part-name", &part)) {
+		part = "cs35l45";
+	} else {
+		/* A board tuning: never run its firmware without the tuning. */
+		cs35l45->dsp_part_named = true;
+		dsp->bin_mandatory = true;
+	}
+	dsp->part = part;
 	dsp->fw = 9; /* 9 is WM_ADSP_FW_SPK_PROT in wm_adsp.c */
 	dsp->toggle_preload = true;
 	dsp->cs_dsp.num = 1;
